      "eyebrow": "Why it matters",
      "heading": "Proof, not memory",
      "html": "<p>The report is not a legal certificate. There is no set form. But it does two jobs. It shows the landlord checked the system. And it records what you found and advised, which protects you if things get worse after you leave.</p><p>Sole traders skip it most. The job is done and the invoice sent. The record then lives only in memory. That is weak if a landlord later says nobody told them about a problem.</p>"
