      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "Common failures",
      "heading": "Timing, vague words, photos",
      "html": "<p>The big problem is when you write it. A pressure reading noted at the test is accurate. One typed three hours later is a guess. That matters if a landlord disputes a low-pressure fault.</p><p>Vague words are next. \"Pipework in reasonable condition\" tells nobody anything. Better: \"Compression joint on 22mm cold supply under kitchen sink, past weeping. Cleaned and tightened. Monitor.\" Last, photos. A photo with a caption beats a description. Attach it at the time.</p>"
    },
