      "html": "<h3>What should a plumbing inspection report include?</h3><p>It should cover visible pipework, joints and fittings, water pressure, leaks and corrosion, drainage, and hot and cold water storage. Add recommended actions, with how urgent each is. Attach photos of defects.</p><h3>Are plumbing inspections a legal requirement for landlords?</h3><p>No single law needs a plumbing certificate like the Gas Safety Record. But the Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 makes landlords keep water, drainage and sanitation installations in repair. A regular inspection is evidence they did.</p><h3>How often should a plumbing inspection be carried out?</h3><p>There is no set interval. Many letting agents suggest every five years for older properties, and at a change of tenancy. Check more often if there is lead pipework, low pressure or known drainage trouble.</p><h3>Can I record pressure test results by voice note?</h3><p>Yes. Say the reading into WhatsApp at the moment of the test. Quickler writes it out for you. See our <a href=\"/pages/inspection-report-template-uk.html\">inspection report template</a> guide.</p>"
